course: dictionary
lesson: 13095
title: Fireproof and the words inside it
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Fire-proof is a word made of two parts: fire and proof. Proof here means "safe from", so fireproof means safe from fire. «The firefighters wore fireproof gloves to lift the hot pan.» The gloves do not burn, so they keep the hands safe. Fireproof means not able to burn or be badly damaged by fire.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The jewels were kept in a fireproof safe during the fire.» A safe is a strong box, and the jewels stayed safe because the box could not be badly damaged by the flames. Ask yourself: what would the jewels need to be safe from? Fire.
explain: The word can also be a verb. «The builders fireproofed the wooden roof with a special treatment.» To fireproof something means to treat it so that it does not catch fire easily. Fireproof, fireproofs, fireproofed and fireproofing are all forms of this one verb.
fact: Fireproof means not able to burn or be badly damaged by fire.
fact: To fireproof something means to treat it so it does not catch fire easily.
fact: «Fireproof» is an adjective when it describes a thing, as in «fireproof gloves».
fact: In science, pupils test which materials burn, and some materials pass the test as fireproof.
fact: A «fire door» is a door built to slow down the spread of fire; it is not the same as a fireproof door.
exercise: «The firefighters wore fireproof gloves to lift the hot pan.» What does fireproof mean? | Very wet and cold | *Not able to burn or be badly damaged by fire | Made of soft cloth | Easy to light
exercise: To fireproof a wooden shed means to | paint it bright red | fill it with water | *treat it so that it does not catch fire easily | knock it down
exercise: «The safe was fireproof, so the papers inside were still safe after the blaze.» Why were the papers still safe? | The safe was locked with a key | The papers were wrapped in plastic bags | The fire was very small | *The safe could not be badly damaged by fire
test: «The school put a fire door at the end of the corridor.» What is a fire door most likely built to do? | Open by itself every morning | Make a loud bell ring | *Slow down the spread of fire | Let in lots of sunshine
test: Which object is most likely to be fireproof? | *A metal safe for important papers | A sheet of tissue paper | A cotton handkerchief | A paper cup
exam: «Scientists tested which materials burn, and the glove did not catch fire at all.» Which word best describes that glove? | Fireside | Soggy | Fireworks | *Fireproof
